+# USDC Pay
+
+Send USDC on Ethereum mainnet from your own wallet. One page, `/pay`: connect,
+enter a recipient and an amount, send — with your USDC and ETH balances in view
+the whole time.
+
+## Stack
+
+- **Next.js 16** (App Router) + TypeScript
+- **wagmi v2 / viem** for chain access
+- **RainbowKit** for wallet connection
+- **TanStack Query** (via wagmi) for caching and refresh
+- **Tailwind CSS v4** for styling
+- **Vitest** for the amount/error logic
+
+## Running it
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # optional, see below
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000/pay
+```
+
+| Script             | What it does                        |
+| ------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
+| `npm run dev`      | Dev server                          |
+| `npm run build`    | Production build (type-checked)     |
+| `npm test`         | Unit tests                          |
+| `npm run lint`     | ESLint                              |
+| `npm run typecheck`| `tsc --noEmit`                      |
+
+### Environment
+
+Both variables are optional locally and **expected in production**:
+
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` — enables WalletConnect and mobile
+  wallets. Without it the app still works, but only offers browser-extension
+  wallets.
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL` — a dedicated mainnet RPC. The public fallback is rate
+  limited and will start dropping balance polls under real traffic.
+
+## How USDC is handled
+
+USDC is [`0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48`](https://etherscan.io/token/0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48)
+on Ethereum mainnet, and it is not a generic ERC-20:
+
+- **6 decimals, not 18.** Every amount is parsed and formatted against
+  `decimals()` read from the contract (with 6 as a fallback), and all math is
+  `bigint` — a 6-decimal balance overflows float precision sooner than you'd
+  think.
+- **Amounts are never silently rewritten.** More than 6 decimal places is an
+  error rather than a rounded-down transfer; a comma is an error rather than a
+  guess between `1,5 = 1.5` and `1,5 = 15`. What's on screen is what gets signed.
+- **Balances truncate, never round up**, so the UI can't show more than the
+  wallet holds.
+- **Every transfer is simulated first** (`eth_call`) before the wallet is asked
+  to sign. USDC is pausable and has a blacklist, so a transfer can fail for
+  reasons no balance check would catch. Those reverts are translated into plain
+  language instead of being discovered after the user has paid for gas.
+- **The token contract can't be the recipient.** Pasting the USDC address into
+  the recipient field is a classic way to lose money permanently; it's blocked,
+  as is the zero address. Sending to a contract, or to yourself, warns instead.
+- **A transaction hash is not a success.** The receipt is awaited and its status
+  checked — a mined-but-reverted transfer is reported as a failure that still
+  cost gas.
+
+## Gas
+
+ETH balance is shown next to USDC because a transfer costs ETH, not USDC. Once
+the form is valid the transfer's gas is estimated and priced at `maxFeePerGas`
+(the worst case), which drives a fee estimate under the amount field, a warning
+when the balance looks too tight to cover it, and a hard block at zero ETH.
+
+## Networks
+
+Mainnet only, deliberately: USDC exists on many chains at different addresses,
+and a "wrong network" bug in a payments UI sends real money to the wrong place.
+Balances are read from mainnet regardless of what the wallet is pointed at, so
+the numbers are never a different chain's; sending is blocked, with a switch
+prompt, until the wallet is on mainnet.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/
+  app/            layout (SSR wallet state), /pay page, providers
+  components/     PayForm, Balances, TxStatus, Header, Notice
+  hooks/          useBalances, useSendUsdc, useRecipient, useDebouncedValue
+  lib/            usdc (address/ABI), amount (parse/format), errors, wagmi config
+```
+
+Balances refresh on every new block and immediately after a transfer is mined.
+Recipient and amount changes are debounced before they hit the network, and a
+send is refused while the simulation is still catching up to the form — so the
+wallet can never be handed a stale amount.
+
+## Not included
+
+No transaction history, no address book, no fiat conversion, no gas-price
+control (the wallet's own controls apply), no batching or `permit`. Sending is
+the whole product.
+
+### One known wart
+
+`next.config.ts` aliases a handful of `@x402/*` module specifiers to a stub.
+They're optional peer dependencies of `@coinbase/cdp-sdk`, which RainbowKit
+pulls in transitively; they're never executed here, but Turbopack fails the
+build on unresolvable imports. The alias is preferable to installing an unused
+payments SDK — revisit whenever RainbowKit or wagmi's connectors update.
